    uac-sweep amd64     both phases, 0 mismatches
    uac-sweep aarch64   both phases, 0 mismatches
    musl 1.2.5          400 sources through mc-tcc, 0 crashes
    memset.S memcpy.S   compile (they segfaulted before the guard)
    ilogb.c ilogbf.c    compile
    case 110            bitmask 3 -> 0
    difftest amd64      105 pass, 0 fail, 0 known gaps
    difftest aarch64    107 pass, 0 fail, 0 known gaps
    stage 2 corpus      420 of 426                       unchanged
    mc-tcc              builds, 1,651,969 bytes
    twelve.sh           12 of 12

The last two matter most: this fires on every arithmetic and relational
operator in the program being compiled, and tcc is full of hex masks above
2^31 compared against signed values. A green case suite would not have said
much on its own.

